v3.8.14
the enclave composes get ETNY_SCONE_QUEUES per network: every docker-compose
  run on an order's or an integration test's compose (pull, down, up) takes
  the agent's environment with the count of the network's PoX generation
  (utils.enclave_compose_env), twice the node's CPUs within 4 and 64 on a
  PoX 1.2 and within 4 and 8 (utils.SCONE_QUEUES_LEGACY_MAX) on a legacy
  PoX, whose trustedzone images are signed without --tcs and take at most
  eight queues; the agent's own environment is no longer given the variable
  (one process serves networks of both generations), and the start line
  "SCONE queues for the enclaves" follows the network's pox= line and names
  the count and the generation. Until now every network got the one count
  of 3.8.11: on a node with 8 CPUs a bloxberg mainnet trustedzone, given 16
  queues, exited with code 1 every 9 seconds (order 22069, 2026-11-19); the
  SCONE runtime's error "Trying to create 16 queues, max allowed: 8" is not
  printed under SCONE_LOG=FATAL

v3.8.13
the capability record's compute figure is gflops, whole GFLOPS of the
  benchmark kernel under cuv 4 (one CU is 100 GFLOPS, utils.GFLOPS_PER_CU):
  the agent admits its own record at cuv CU_VERSION_MIN (4) and above with
  gflops at most CU_MAX_GFLOPS (6400, CU_MAX 64 x 100), the gflops bound
  checked first as the validators check it; a stored record (in
  node/<network>/capability.json) below CU_VERSION_MIN or without gflops is
  dropped when the store loads, the test's pass kept with retest_pending set
  in the file until the next pass (RecordStore.retest_pending), and its
  integration test runs again, after a restart as well; an admitted record is
  logged as "record admitted (gflops N (x.xx CU), cuv M, ..."
addDPRequestV2 carries the record's gflops (0 without a record, recorded by
  the contract at 100), metadata4 carries cugflops=<gflops>, and the tip per
  CU-hour spreads the node's own gas over gflops / 100 CU
  (utils.tip_per_cu_hour_wei); the pre-filter refuses a V2 DO request whose
  maxGflops is below the node's gflops (Refusal kind gflops, cached), and the
  placement refusal "node above maxGflops" names the offer
the validators' cancel reasons 6 GflopsAboveMax and 8 CuVersionBelowMinimum
  (capability.CANCEL_REASONS) re-test the record before the re-add
  (RETEST_REASONS 1..6, 8 and 9); 7 DeliveredBelowAttested re-adds
the validators' cancel reason 9 RecordMissing (an offer without a capability
  record that the validators do not pass over: its trustedzones= list names
  none, names a trustedzone without the -unsafe suffix, or the network admits
  no -unsafe trustedzone)
  sets the network's RecordMissing hold (capability.RecordMissingHold, kept
  under record_missing_hold in node/<network>/broker_cursor.json, written
  before the scan's cursor moves, so a restart keeps it): the agent posts no
  DP request without a record on that network unless the request names only
  -unsafe trustedzones (capability.unsafe_only, the offer the validators pass
  over) (add_dp_request, the request sent with a result and the idle tick's
  replacement), logs the hold once per change and waits
  RECORD_MISSING_POLL_SECONDS (60) between its looks for a record, running
  meanwhile the idle duties that need no standing request (the heartbeat,
  the IPFS cleanup and peering, an order approved after its window, the
  broker's tick); the passed tests whose image requires dcap and whose pass
  holds no record run again at once, and while they pass without one they
  run again on the failure backoff (10 min doubling to 6 h); an advertised
  record clears the hold and the request carries it. A network whose
  validators never cancelled with reason 9 has no hold, and its agent posts
  a request without a record (where the validators do not vote, as on LitVM,
  it stands)
the DPRequestCancelled scan reads the cancels of every DP request of the
  node (the indexed dproc topic) from the persisted dp_request_cancelled
  cursor, before every add (a process start's first included, so a cancel
  that landed while the agent was stopped is seen) and at every idle tick;
  the reaction follows the record the cancelled request carried
  (capability.cancel_reaction over its cusig, RecordStore.image_of): a
  record reason on a request that carried a record drops that record and
  re-tests, a request without a record has none to drop
the bundled ABI files node/docker/pox.abi, node/reader.abi, node/pricing.abi
  and node/broker.abi are the pox-smart-contract-litvm exports with the GFLOPS
  names (gflops, maxGflops, minGflops, gflopsMax, gflopsMaxDefault,
  capacityGflops, loadGflops, reservedGflops, reservedCapacityGflops); the
  agent reads them as DORequestV2.max_gflops, DPTerms.gflops and
  OrderTerms.gflops, and accepted.json holds predecessor_gflops
  (broker.bounded_gflops)
bloxberg_testnet and bloxberg_testnet_unsafe bind the PoX 1.2 implementation
  0x830c781F0352050343211B6BFA83600B3e77647C, polygon_amoy and
  polygon_amoy_unsafe the PoX 1.2 implementation
  0xd1182deA61CDa785C320cdBE5888EaC4178cAAF2 (node/.env): the
  implementations of pox-smart-contract-litvm deployed 2026-11-18, whose
  compute figures are whole GFLOPS

v3.8.12
the payload intake (ipfs_intake.py, the bootnode's ipfs.ethernity.cloud
  /payload) serves a runner in a web page under the browser's cross-origin
  rules (CORS): it answers the OPTIONS preflight with 204 and
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *, Access-Control-Allow-Methods: POST, OPTIONS,
  Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, Content-Length,
  X-Etny-Owner-Signature and Access-Control-Max-Age: 86400, and every reply,
  refusals included, carries Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *, so the page reads
  the status and the body (until now the preflight was answered 501 and the
  browser blocked the upload)

v3.8.11
the agent exports ETNY_SCONE_QUEUES, twice the node's CPUs within 4 and 64
  (utils.scone_queues), into its own environment at start, and the enclave
  composes of the trustedzone and the securelock substitute it into
  SCONE_QUEUES (the enclave threads each image runs its application threads
  on; the images are signed with 64 TCS and ship four queues as the floor);
  the trustedzone's benchmark runs the same count of workers (inside the
  enclave SCONE reports the queues as the CPUs), so a node's cu is measured
  on all its cores (benchmark.json cuv 3: workersPerCpu 1, workersMax 64,
  the probe at the full 50,000 rounds)

v3.8.10
the reward banner after a result names, on a recorded 1.2 order, the node's
  payout from the settlement (the reader's settlementOf: work plus the chain
  gas repaid, utils.settlement_reward_wei, four decimals) instead of the DO
  request's price less the legacy fees, which a 1.2 order no longer pays
  (bloxberg testnet order 23: "Reward: 2.55 tETNY" beside a settlement of
  0.2002 tETNY of work); a legacy order keeps its figure

v3.8.9
