v3.8.4
the passed integration test reads the tree's compose by its absolute path
  when it keeps the tested LAS, and a compose it cannot read leaves the LAS
  unkept with a warning instead of failing the pass; the process's working
  directory is shared by the network threads, which move it to their own
  node/<network>/

v3.8.3
an order's enclaves run with the LAS of a trustedzone tree that passed this
  node's integration test instead of the LAS bundled in the dApp's own tree:
  the pass keeps the tree's las service block in
  node/<network>/las-tested-<trustedzone>.yml and its image under the docker
  tag localhost:5000/etny-las:tested-<trustedzone>, the order's compose takes
  that block's entrypoint and command and its LAS image name is pointed at
  the tested image (logged "The LAS of <trustedzone>'s tested tree runs this
  order's enclaves"); a trustedzone without a test of its own takes the
  tested LAS of one with the same platform requirement; a recorded pass
  loaded at start without a kept LAS runs its test again; an order whose
  trustedzone has no tested LAS held by docker runs its tree's own. The LAS
  is in no enclave's measurement

v3.8.2
the DP request sent behind an order's result, and the one sent after a
  cancel, carry DP_REQUEST_GAS_HEADROOM_PERCENT (25) over their gas estimate
  on an EIP-1559 network: the estimate is made at the head block and the
  request is mined in a later one, where the call needs up to 1.5 % more
  (Amoy)
a DO request refused for its resources is held in
  node/<network>/doreq_resources.json with the four it needs and judged again
  once this node's offer serves it; a request refused before 3.8.2 stays in
  doreq_cache.txt; the file is removed with the other request caches when the
  network's contract changes

